# P6 adversarial pass

Root cause (6de1d0e, crates/ovis-terminal-cli/src/assembly/live.rs:186-187):
    live.waits.ingest(output)?;          // the waits' own Screen; resolves tickets
    let replies = live.hub.publish(output)?;   // the attach hub's Screen
terminal.wait_output awaits its ticket on spawn_blocking (assembly/waited.rs settled/routes.rs:86)
and replies as soon as waits.ingest resolves it, while the actor thread has not yet run
hub.publish. attach.repaint is served by AttachHandler::stream_call -> TerminalStreams::repaint
(server/src/streams/handler.rs:197, ops.rs:70) under the hub lock only, not on the actor, so it
can paint the hub's screen before the matched chunk lands. The hub's tracker then still holds
the CSI opened by "OPEN\e[3\r" (tainted by the \r) -> inexact [control_inside_open_sequence],
exactly the CI actual at step 130. terminal.screen / terminal.output read the same hub screen
(assembly/reads.rs), so they had the same window. Nothing in fcfd5e5..6de1d0e touched this
order; the hypothesis that the repaint snapshot point moved in replay.rs/read.rs was checked
and rejected (those hunks add placeholders/index reads only).

Fix: assembly/live/commit.rs commits each chunk to the hub first, then to the waits; the exit
is recorded on the hub, then on the waits. Ordering, not serialization: no lock is added and
repaint is still served off the actor.

Classes probed:
1. Reversed order (m1 = 6de1d0e order): unit test a_chunk_the_hub_refuses_resolves_no_wait FAILS;
   scenario attach-input/repaint-after-wait (500 ms QA gap) FAILS 3/3 with the CI symptom
   (inexact [control_inside_open_sequence], checkpoint output_offset 8 < 14). See mutants.log,
   regression.log.
2. Waits never fed (m2): a_matched_wait_finds_its_bytes_already_in_the_hub_paint FAILS.
3. Refused chunk leaks to waits (m3, hub error deferred past waits.ingest): a_chunk_the_hub_refuses_resolves_no_wait FAILS.
4. Masking by tty echo: the echo of "go" puts 'g' (a CSI final byte) on the wire and closes the
   sequence in an earlier chunk, so a reversed order can still paint exact. The first
   regression-scenario draft (echo on, wait armed after the input) PASSED on m1; the shipped
   scenario runs `stty -echo` and asserts checkpoint output_offset >= 14 as well as inexact [].
5. Masking by wait arming order: a wait armed after the closing bytes matches from retained
   output on the actor (both screens already fed) and cannot race. The shipped scenario sends
   terminal.wait_output before input.send.
6. QA seam abuse: --qa-output-commit-gap-ms is refused off a QA fixture root (serve.rs
   qa_seams_allowed); the protocol fixture refuses the scenario key (ScenarioInconsistent).
7. Exit ordering (hub.finish before waits.finish) is not covered by a failing test: both screens
   refuse an exit identically, so no single-threaded test separates the orders. Listed as a risk.
8. Load: 6de1d0e under taskset -c 0-1 + 8 busy loops never reaches step 130 (step 54 flood wait
   times out every run, before-loaded-loop.log); all/all 5x on 4 loaded cores: attach-input/* 5/5,
   two runs miss capacity/sixteen's 100 ms admission bound, which the 6de1d0e and this branch's
   binaries both pass 5/5 when task-30 runs alone under the same load (after-loaded-all.log).
